---
title: Chocolate Custard Pie
tags:
  - desserts
source:
  name: Serious Eats
  url: https://www.seriouseats.com/chocolate-cream-pie-meringue-recipe/
---

Prepare a blind-baked @./cook/pie-dough{1}.

Combine @72% dark chocolate chips{115%grams} and @vanilla extract{7%grams} in a mixing bowl and place a metal strainer over the top (resting on the bowl).

Whisk @granulated sugar{135%grams}, @kosher salt{1%tsp}, @Dutch-process cocoa{45%grams}, and @cornstarch{35%grams} together in a medium, heavy pot.

Add @egg yolks{140%grams} and @heavy cream{1%cup}, whisk until smooth.

Cook over medium heat, stirring continuously until hot and solids are dissolved (about ~{6%minutes}).

Add @milk{2%cups}.

Increase heat and continue whisking until thick and bubbly.

Whisk for another ~{90%seconds} after the first bubbling.

Pour into the chocolate chip bowl through the sieve, pressing as needed to pass the custard through.

Fold into the chocolate chips until everything is mixed.

Let cool, then pour into the blind-baked crust.

Chill in the refrigerator. Add @./cook/whipped-cream{1} if you like before serving.